WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.554
Hi! A grammar cloze is a short passage with several blanks, and you fill them with words from a box. Today we'll learn how.

2
00:00:10.704 --> 00:00:16.002
First read the whole passage to know the story and whether it's past or present.

3
00:00:16.152 --> 00:00:20.178
For each ___, look at the words before and after it.

4
00:00:20.328 --> 00:00:26.610
Ask: does it need a preposition, a pronoun, a conjunction, or a verb form?

5
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:32.586
Cross out used words in the box, and read the passage again at the end.

6
00:00:32.736 --> 00:00:37.122
Yesterday or last week means the verb is in the past tense.

7
00:00:37.272 --> 00:00:42.402
Choose by position: he before the verb, him after it, his for owning.

8
00:00:42.552 --> 00:00:45.978
Use at, on and in for times and places.

9
00:00:46.128 --> 00:00:51.162
Choose a conjunction by how the two ideas are linked.

10
00:00:51.312 --> 00:00:57.330
Watch out! If you don't read the whole passage, you may forget the story is in the past!

11
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.314
Last Sunday shows the past, so go becomes went.

12
00:01:01.464 --> 00:01:06.834
For every ___, first ask: when did this happen?

13
00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:16.554
Your turn! Mei, ___, her teeth every night. Which one? Pause and think.

14
00:01:16.704 --> 00:01:23.778
Every night is a habit and Mei is one person, so brushes. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:23.928 --> 00:01:34.866
Another one! Ravi lost, ___, pencil, so he borrowed mine. Which one? Pause and think.

16
00:01:35.016 --> 00:01:41.610
A noun, pencil, follows, and it's his, so his. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:51.378
Here's another! The party is, ___, Saturday. Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:56.130
Days take on. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:05.994
Try one more! It was late, ___, we went home. Which one? Pause and think.

20
00:02:06.144 --> 00:02:12.354
Being late is the reason, it comes first, so so. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:12.504 --> 00:02:23.082
Try one more! Yesterday the children, ___, a sandcastle. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:23.232 --> 00:02:29.970
Yesterday means past, and the past of build is built. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:39.882
Try one more! There, ___, many books on the shelf. Which one? Pause and think.

24
00:02:40.032 --> 00:02:45.186
Books is plural, so are. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:45.336 --> 00:02:55.314
Last one! Look! The baby, ___, now. Which one? Pause and think.

26
00:02:55.464 --> 00:03:01.866
Look and now tell us it is happening, so is sleeping. Did you get it right?

27
00:03:02.016 --> 00:03:12.258
Remember: read the whole passage, look before and after each ___, decide what kind of word fits, cross out used words, and read it again at the end.

28
00:03:12.408 --> 00:03:17.898
When you finish, read it aloud and listen: does it sound right?

